{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_24", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc \"cat > /tmp/research_history/build_lowrank_episode3.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nroot=Path('/tmp/research_history');base=(root/'086_recurrent_torch_kernel/method.py').read_text()\na=base.index('def _expectation(');b=base.index('def _outer(')\nold=base[a:b].replace('def _expectation(C):','def _dense_expectation(C):')\nfor num,k in [(96,32),(97,64),(98,96)]:\n code=old+f'''def _expectation(C,a,b,yl,rl,W):\n    n,m=C.shape\n    k=min({k},n,m)\n    ii=torch.from_numpy(np.linspace(0,n-1,k,dtype=np.int64))\n    jj=torch.from_numpy(np.linspace(0,m-1,k,dtype=np.int64))\n    eps=.1*float(C.max())\n    kc=torch.exp(C[:,jj]/(-eps))\n    kr=torch.exp(C[ii,:]/(-eps))\n    core=kc[ii,:]\n    L=kc @ torch.linalg.pinv(core,rtol=1e-6)\n    R=kr\n    u=torch.full((n,),1./n);v=torch.full((m,),1./m)\n    for it in range(3):\n        vm=R.T @ (L.T @ u)\n        if float(vm.min())<=0.:return _dense_expectation(C)\n        v=(1./m)/vm\n        um=L @ (R @ v)\n        if float(um.min())<=0.:return _dense_expectation(C)\n        u=(1./n)/um\n    A=torch.from_numpy(a);B=torch.from_numpy(b)\n    E=torch.cat(((A*A).sum(1)[:,None]/2,torch.ones((n,1)),A,torch.from_numpy(W)[torch.from_numpy(yl),10:]/2),1)\n    H=torch.cat((torch.ones((m,1)),(B*B).sum(1)[:,None]/2,-B,torch.nn.functional.one_hot(torch.from_numpy(rl),10).float()),1)\n    return float(((L.T @ (u[:,None]*E))*(R @ (v[:,None]*H))).sum())\n\n\n'''\n src=base[:a]+code+base[b:]\n src=src.replace('_expectation(T)/(len(idx)+len(jdx))','_expectation(T,a,b,y[idx],ry[jdx],W)/(len(idx)+len(jdx))')\n d=root/f'{num:03d}_lowrank_coupling_{k}';d.mkdir(exist_ok=True);(d/'method.py').write_text(src)\nPY\npython /tmp/research_history/build_lowrank_episode3.py\ncat >> /tmp/research_history/episode_3_working_notes.md <<'EOF'\n\n## 085-089 initial tests\n-085 NumPy kernel recurrence and086 Torch recurrence algebraically reuse the shared kernel across quartered temperatures: divide by geometric row/column mean factors and square twice. Retain stable dense transform fallback if positive mass fails. Both local30 pass, worst nRMSE .00315694/.00315688. Mean local times .18712/.14875.086 sent to real evaluator alone.\n-087/088/089 take deterministic stride2/4/8 supports for the coupling. All fail all30; worst nRMSE .15911/.34832/.52394. Dense coupling cannot be replaced by raw subsampling.\n-Next variants090 recycle the initialization kernel,091 apply recurrence to empirical class kernels,092 combine.093-095 coupling exponential binomial expansion ablates approximation to broad entropy kernel.096-098 use CUR rank32/64/96 coupling kernels with analytic rank22 cost contraction; all derive supports and factors from inputs. None of these screened or retained yet.\nEOF\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
